  "notes": "{溢|あふ}れる is an intransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}) describing overflow or abundance.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{溢|あふ}れている indicates something is currently overflowing or full of something.\n\nPARTICLE PATTERNS:\n- [container]から[liquid]が{溢|あふ}れる — [liquid] overflows from [container]\n- [quality]に{溢|あふ}れる — to be full of [quality]\n- [place]に[things]が{溢|あふ}れる — [place] is overflowing with [things]\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {涙|なみだ}が{溢|あふ}れる (tears overflow)\n- {愛情|あいじょう}に{溢|あふ}れる (full of affection)\n- {活気|かっき}に{溢|あふ}れる (full of vitality)\n- {笑顔|えがお}に{溢|あふ}れる (full of smiles)\n\nOFTEN WRITTEN IN HIRAGANA:\nThis verb is frequently written as あふれる rather than {溢|あふ}れる due to the kanji's complexity.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {零|こぼ}れる: to spill (smaller amounts, drops)\n- {溢|あふ}れる: to overflow (larger amounts, abundance)",
